:::

:::details 2. Brute force: list of words grouped by length
Bucket words by length so only same-length words are compared, then check each one position by position, treating `.` as a match.

**Java**

```java
class WordDictionary {
    private final Map<Integer, List<String>> byLen = new HashMap<>(); // words grouped by length

    public WordDictionary() {}

    public void addWord(String word) {
        byLen.computeIfAbsent(word.length(), k -> new ArrayList<>()).add(word);
    }

    public boolean search(String word) {
        for (String w : byLen.getOrDefault(word.length(), List.of())) {
            boolean ok = true;
            for (int i = 0; i < w.length() && ok; i++)
                if (word.charAt(i) != '.' && word.charAt(i) != w.charAt(i)) ok = false;
            if (ok) return true;
        }
        return false;
    }
}
