**Space:** O(n) recursion (output excluded)
:::

:::details 2. Iterative (BFS-style product)
Start with `[""]`. For each digit, replace the list with every existing prefix extended by every letter of that digit.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    private static final String[] KEYS = {"", "", "abc", "def", "ghi", "jkl", "mno", "pqrs", "tuv", "wxyz"};

    public List<String> letterCombinations(String digits) {
        if (digits.isEmpty()) return new ArrayList<>();
        List<String> res = new ArrayList<>(List.of(""));
        for (char d : digits.toCharArray()) {
            List<String> next = new ArrayList<>();
            for (String prefix : res)
                for (char ch : KEYS[d - '0'].toCharArray()) next.add(prefix + ch);
            res = next;
        }
        return res;
    }
}
```

