:::

:::details 2. DFS from each gate with relaxation
From each gate, DFS outward carrying the distance `d`, and only continue into a cell if `d` is smaller than what it holds. Correct, but a room can be overwritten many times as closer gates are found later.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public void wallsAndGates(int[][] rooms) {
        for (int r = 0; r < rooms.length; r++)
            for (int c = 0; c < rooms[0].length; c++)
                if (rooms[r][c] == 0) dfs(rooms, r, c, 0);
    }

    // only continue if this path improves the cell's distance
    private void dfs(int[][] rooms, int r, int c, int d) {
        if (r < 0 || c < 0 || r >= rooms.length || c >= rooms[0].length || rooms[r][c] < d) return;
        rooms[r][c] = d;
        dfs(rooms, r + 1, c, d + 1);
        dfs(rooms, r - 1, c, d + 1);
        dfs(rooms, r, c + 1, d + 1);
        dfs(rooms, r, c - 1, d + 1);
    }
}
```

