:::

:::details 3. Brute force: BFS from every room
For each empty room, BFS until the first gate and write its distance. Repeats the same exploration for neighbouring rooms.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public void wallsAndGates(int[][] rooms) {
        for (int r = 0; r < rooms.length; r++)
            for (int c = 0; c < rooms[0].length; c++)
                if (rooms[r][c] == Integer.MAX_VALUE) rooms[r][c] = nearestGate(rooms, r, c);
    }

    private int nearestGate(int[][] rooms, int sr, int sc) {
        int rows = rooms.length, cols = rooms[0].length;
        boolean[][] seen = new boolean[rows][cols];
        Deque<int[]> q = new ArrayDeque<>();
        q.add(new int[]{sr, sc, 0});
        seen[sr][sc] = true;
        int[][] dirs = {{1, 0}, {-1, 0}, {0, 1}, {0, -1}};
        while (!q.isEmpty()) {
            int[] e = q.poll();
            if (rooms[e[0]][e[1]] == 0) return e[2];
            for (int[] d : dirs) {
                int nr = e[0] + d[0], nc = e[1] + d[1];
                if (nr >= 0 && nc >= 0 && nr < rows && nc < cols && rooms[nr][nc] != -1 && !seen[nr][nc]) {
                    seen[nr][nc] = true;
                    q.add(new int[]{nr, nc, e[2] + 1});
                }
            }
        }
        return Integer.MAX_VALUE;
    }
}
```

