:::details 2. Multi-source BFS from the border
Same marking with a queue seeded with every border `O`. Avoids deep recursion on large boards.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public void solve(char[][] board) {
        int rows = board.length, cols = board[0].length;
        Deque<int[]> q = new ArrayDeque<>();
        for (int r = 0; r < rows; r++)
            for (int c = 0; c < cols; c++)
                if ((r == 0 || c == 0 || r == rows - 1 || c == cols - 1) && board[r][c] == 'O') {
                    board[r][c] = 'S';
                    q.add(new int[]{r, c});
                }
        int[][] dirs = {{1, 0}, {-1, 0}, {0, 1}, {0, -1}};
        while (!q.isEmpty()) {
            int[] cell = q.poll();
            for (int[] d : dirs) {
                int nr = cell[0] + d[0], nc = cell[1] + d[1];
                if (nr >= 0 && nc >= 0 && nr < rows && nc < cols && board[nr][nc] == 'O') {
                    board[nr][nc] = 'S';
                    q.add(new int[]{nr, nc});
                }
            }
        }
        for (int r = 0; r < rows; r++)
            for (int c = 0; c < cols; c++)
                board[r][c] = board[r][c] == 'S' ? 'O' : 'X';
    }
}
```

